# Toy control (D-85, D-119; code review WR-02): the first rule of the pc field of a device-register record, which read the pc of the instance when the record was written, made from the live src/core/bus.c by scripts/control-mutate. The anchor is the argument of the one ds_obs_dev
# call that names the pc the bus carries; the replacement reads the instance instead, which is the address after the transfer for every byte and epilogue step of a block transfer (the prologue moves the program counter past the seven bytes). The case in EXPECT must come out guest_failure on
# the toy, or no case can see that the dev records of a TII carry the next instruction's address. The real core passes it (a REQUIRED case).
tag=rule-dev-pc-from-instance
file=src/core/bus.c
anchor=stamp, bus->pc, HW_PAGE_PHYS | offset,
replace=stamp, (uint32_t)inst->pc, HW_PAGE_PHYS | offset,
